# Rule: production parity

Read this before you change the container files, deploy configuration, build configuration, a package manifest or the lockfile. (Claude Code loads it through `.claude/rules/production-parity.md`.)

Production is the container image, booted by its entrypoint on the host. Development runs on the developer's machine. These differences can break production while everything passes locally:

| # | Dev to production | Rule |
|---|---|---|
| P1 | All dependencies installed, to production-only dependencies | Anything the server or entrypoint runs at runtime is a runtime dependency, not a dev dependency. |
| P2 | Whole repo, to only the files the image copies | Runtime code reads only copied files. A new runtime file needs a copy step in the image. |
| P3 | Local env files, to the host's variables | Scripts that run in the container never assume dev-only files or flags. See `env-and-secrets.md`. |

